    <Folder>
      <name>Photo landmarks · sheet order</name>
      <open>1</open>
      <Placemark>
        <name>MRT Buendia / Zodiac · Jupiter junction</name>
        <description>Zodiac Street meets Jupiter here near MRT Buendia. Both archived lines reach this junction. The 2022 queue location is unknown.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/2225262309"&gt;Position source&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://lawphil.net/executive/proc/proc2008/proc_1618_2008.html"&gt;Proclamation 1618: Zodiac, Jupiter and Gil Puyat&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>121.035011,14.5559253</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Jupiter Street / Makati Avenue</name>
        <description>The pin marks the intersection. Identify the boarding corner before linking a stop.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/6622257246"&gt;Position source&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://verification.fda.gov.ph/ALL_DRUG_INDUSTRYview.php?ACCOUNTCODE=CDRR-NCR-DS-46075&amp;amp;export=pdf"&gt;Philippine FDA address at the corner&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>121.0281673,14.5620699</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Lopez Drive / Estrella–Pantaleon Bridge</name>
        <description>The pin represents the mapped bridge footprint. Both archived lines pass the Makati approach and cross the Pasig farther west on the Makati–Mandaluyong Bridge. The sheet gives no exact Lopez Drive stop.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/664779807"&gt;Position source&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://mirror.pia.gov.ph/press-releases/2021/07/30/president-duterte-opens-estrella-pantaleon-bridge"&gt;DPWH bridge approaches&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://www.tourism.gov.ph/asean2026/"&gt;Lopez Drive in Rockwell Center&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>121.0376601,14.566831</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>City of Mandaluyong Science High School</name>
        <description>The pin represents the school grounds on E. Pantaleon Street in Hulo. The entrance and waiting area need field confirmation.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/17310343"&gt;Position source&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://mandaluyong.gov.ph/profile/education/"&gt;City school directory&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>121.0354326,14.5687816</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Tivoli Garden Residences</name>
        <description>DMCI Homes places the property here on Coronado Street. Both archived lines turn away before the later Tivoli platforms. The 2022 boarding location is unknown.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.dmcihomes.com/tivoli-garden-residences"&gt;Position source&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>121.03118,14.57174</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Maysilo Circle / Mandaluyong City Hall</name>
        <description>This road node on the circle appears in both archived lines. The sheet identifies the City Hall complex. The 2022 loading bay is unknown.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/25584004"&gt;Position source&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://mandaluyongcitycouncil.com/location"&gt;City Council location&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>121.0344662,14.5781694</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
